The most important part of the response is the following:

<script>
var isAdmin = false;
if (isAdmin) {
   var topLinksTag = document.getElementsByClassName("top-links")[0];
   var adminPanelTag = document.createElement('a');
   adminPanelTag.setAttribute('href', '/admin-RandomID');
   adminPanelTag.innerText = 'Admin panel';
   topLinksTag.append(adminPanelTag);
   var pTag = document.createElement('p');
   pTag.innerText = '|';
   topLinksTag.appendChild(pTag);
}
</script>

This script puts a link to the admin panel on the user interface if the user is a administrator, but this script can be seen by any user that request the login page, the location is in the line:

adminPanelTag.setAttribute('href', '/admin-RandomID');

I changed the real ID of the page with the word "RandomID", i believe is different for everybody but i decided it was better to obfuscate the ID. After this, i just request the page on my browser with the following URL:

https://LAB_ID.web-security-academy.net/admin-RandomID

and the admin panel with the users show up, to solve the lab, i just delete the user Carlos.


